cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ADMIT Bench in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ADMIT Bench: An Admissibility Standard for AI Agents that Act on Physical Plants"
abstract: >-
  ADMIT Bench (Admissible Decisions for Machine Interventions) is an
  admissibility-first evaluation benchmark for industrial AI agents. It grades
  each proposed agent action as a trace-backed state transition through a
  deterministic chain of safety gates before any performance score exists; a
  failed hard gate yields no aggregate, so unsafe behavior is ineligible for
  ranking rather than ranked low.
